DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261018T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261018T183000
SUMMARY:Brandywine Valley Happy Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 join us for this lovely point-to-point hike in Chester County\, Pennsylvan
 ia\, featuring more of the diverse trails and back roads in the vicinity o
 f the Brandywine Creek.\nAfter meeting at our endpoint\, Shaw's Bridge Par
 k\, we will shuttle with as few cars as possible to our beginning Point ne
 ar Downingtown to begin our 15 or 16 mile hike.\nThe first portion of this
  will be on the regular Brandywine Trail\, and then we'll make our way up 
 to Harmony Hill. between Harmony Hill\, Starr Farm\, and a couple of other
  Parks\, we will cover. probably about 7 miles.\nwe'll make our way down t
 o a few country roads and skip a piece of the Brandywine Trail that was no
 t maintained from a previous hike\, and then headed to the Stroud Preserve
 .\nwe'll watch the miles to determine how much we do there\, and then make
  our way south a bit more on some back roads to Shaw's Bridge.\nThis will 
 probably be the last hike in our Brandywine series for the season\, and wi
 ll head back when the weather gets warm again.\nThere are no stores of any
  kind on this hike\, so everyone should come prepared with all the food an
 d water they need for this one.\nIf needed\, contact me at 9083438374
